    "prompt": "Function `_arrange_dock_widgets` in src/textual/_arrange.py. The statements below were written about this exact version of the function.\n\nFunction source (docstring removed):\n```python\ndef _arrange_dock_widgets(\n    dock_widgets: Sequence[Widget], region: Region, viewport: Size\n) -> tuple[list[WidgetPlacement], Spacing]:\n    _WidgetPlacement = WidgetPlacement\n    top_z = TOP_Z\n    region_offset = region.offset\n    size = region.size\n    width, height = size\n    null_spacing = Spacing()\n\n    top = right = bottom = left = 0\n\n    placements: list[WidgetPlacement] = []\n    append_placement = placements.append\n\n    for dock_widget in dock_widgets:\n        edge = dock_widget.styles.dock\n\n        box_model = dock_widget._get_box_model(\n            size, viewport, Fraction(size.width), Fraction(size.height)\n        )\n        widget_width_fraction, widget_height_fraction, margin = box_model\n        widget_width = int(widget_width_fraction) + margin.width\n        widget_height = int(widget_height_fraction) + margin.height\n\n        if edge == \"bottom\":\n            dock_region = Region(0, height - widget_height, widget_width, widget_height)\n            bottom = max(bottom, widget_height)\n        elif edge == \"top\":\n            dock_region = Region(0, 0, widget_width, widget_height)\n            top = max(top, widget_height)\n        elif edge == \"left\":\n            dock_region = Region(0, 0, widget_width, widget_height)\n            left = max(left, widget_width)\n        elif edge == \"right\":\n            dock_region = Region(width - widget_width, 0, widget_width, widget_height)\n            right = max(right, widget_width)\n        else:\n            # Should not occur, mainly to keep Mypy happy\n            raise AssertionError(\"invalid value for dock edge\")  # pragma: no-cover\n\n        align_offset = dock_widget.styles._align_size(\n            (widget_width, widget_height), size\n        )\n        dock_region = dock_region.shrink(margin).translate(align_offset)\n        append_placement(\n            _WidgetPlacement(\n                dock_region.translate(region_offset),\n                null_spacing,\n                dock_widget,\n                top_z,\n                True,\n            )\n        )\n    dock_spacing = Spacing(top, right, bottom, left)\n    return (placements, dock_spacing)\n```\n\nFacts extracted from this version by a parser (tree-sitter):\nsignature: _arrange_dock_widgets(dock_widgets, region, viewport) -> tuple[list[WidgetPlacement], Spacing]\ncalls: AssertionError, Fraction, Region, Spacing, _WidgetPlacement, append_placement, dock_region.shrink, dock_region.shrink(margin).translate, dock_region.translate, dock_widget._get_box_model, dock_widget.styles._align_size, int, max\nreturn statements: return (placements, dock_spacing)\nraise statements: raise AssertionError(\"invalid value for dock edge\")\ncontrol flow: if=1 loops=1 try=0 with=0 returns=1 yields=0 awaits=0\n\n\nStatements:\nS1. The `_arrange_dock_widgets` function takes three parameters: `dock_widgets`, `region`, and `viewport`.\nS2. The `dock_widgets` parameter is a sequence of widgets to be arranged.\nS3. The `region` parameter is a Region object defining the area where widgets will be placed.\nS4. The `viewport` parameter is a Size object representing the viewport dimensions.\nS5. The function returns a tuple containing a list of WidgetPlacement objects and a Spacing object.\nS6. The function relies on helper methods like `_get_box_model` to compute widget dimensions and margins.\nS7. The function relies on helper methods like `_align_size` to align widgets within the region.\nS8. If an invalid docking edge is encountered, the function raises an AssertionError.\nS9. The function does not have any side effects; it only computes and returns the arrangement without modifying external state.\nS10. The `_arrange_dock_widgets` function calculates the placement and spacing for each widget based on its docking edge and alignment within the region.\nS11. The function considers the viewport size when arranging the dock widgets.\nS12. The purpose of the `_arrange_dock_widgets` function is to arrange a sequence of dock widgets within a specified region, considering the viewport size.\n\nFor each statement decide:\n- supported: the shown code makes the statement true (a statement about purpose/intent counts as supported unless the code contradicts it).\n- contradicted: the shown code clearly makes the statement false, e.g. a named parameter, call, attribute, return value, exception or condition it describes no longer exists or now behaves differently.\n- unresolved: the statement concerns code that is not shown (callers, helper internals, external systems) and the shown code neither confirms nor refutes it.\nBe strict about \"contradicted\": require concrete evidence in the shown code or the diff; renaming a local variable or reformatting does not contradict a statement about behaviour.\n\nAnswer with exactly one line per statement and nothing else, in this format:\nS1: supported\nS2: contradicted -- <evidence, at most 12 words>\nS3: unresolved",
